{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Rb8FsCmmLsvUatAeBX3pBc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: implement-change\n3\tdescription: Use when you take a MantisBT task (bug fix or small feature) from description to a verified change, using the fast and full gates.\n4\t---\n5\t\n6\t# Implement a change in MantisBT\n7\t\n8\t1. Find the issue on https://mantisbt.org/bugs. Every pull request must reference one (CONTRIBUTING.md). Note its number for the PR description (`Fixes #NNNN`, see `.github/pull_request_template.md`).\n9\t2. Make sure the tools are ready: `composer run setup`. It installs Composer and npm dependencies and the pre-push hook.\n10\t3. Locate the code. Use [docs/product.md](../../../docs/product.md) to map the use case to its entry points, and [docs/architecture.md](../../../docs/architecture.md) for the layers. Business rules go in `core/commands/` or `core/*_api.php`, not in a root page.\n11\t4. Write or extend a test first:\n12\t   - Pure logic that does not need `core.php`: add a test in `tests/Unit/` and run `vendor/bin/phpunit -c phpunit.unit.xml --filter <TestName>`.\n13\t   - Logic that needs the database: add a test in `tests/Mantis/` (extends `MantisCoreBase`). REST behaviour goes in `tests/rest/`.\n14\t5. Make the change. Follow the conventions in AGENTS.md: tabs, `p_`/`t_`/`c_`/`f_`/`g_` prefixes, `require_api()` for core modules, user-visible text through `lang_get()` (see the `add-language-string` skill).\n15\t6. Run the fast gate: `composer run check-fast`. Fix every failure. Do not skip or delete tests.\n16\t7. If the change touches the database, a command, the REST or SOAP API, or a page flow, run the full gate: `composer run check` (needs Docker, reinstalls the local instance). To run one integration test after an install: `vendor/bin/phpunit --filter <TestName>`.\n17\t8. If the schema changes, add an upgrade step at the end of `admin/schema.php`. Never edit existing steps.\n18\t9. Commit with a short imperative subject, as the history does (`Fix tag cache invalidation`, then `Test tag cache invalidation`).\n19\t10. Add an entry to `docs/harness/log.md` if you learned something that the next person needs. Open a pull request to `master`. Never push to `master` directly.\n20\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"664bf491-d717-4ffc-91aa-ea6766d2102e","uuid":"62d27059-d7f3-49f2-abf2-40976592085d","timestamp":"2026-11-01T19:07:41.027Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/victor/Repos/unwritten/uw-harness-cases/mantisbt/repo/.agents/skills/implement-change/SKILL.md","content":"---\nname: implement-change\ndescription: Use when you take a MantisBT task (bug fix or small feature) from description to a verified change, using the fast and full gates.\n---\n\n# Implement a change in MantisBT\n\n1. Find the issue on https://mantisbt.org/bugs. Every pull request must reference one (CONTRIBUTING.md). Note its number for the PR description (`Fixes #NNNN`, see `.github/pull_request_template.md`).\n2. Make sure the tools are ready: `composer run setup`. It installs Composer and npm dependencies and the pre-push hook.\n3. Locate the code. Use [docs/product.md](../../../docs/product.md) to map the use case to its entry points, and [docs/architecture.md](../../../docs/architecture.md) for the layers. Business rules go in `core/commands/` or `core/*_api.php`, not in a root page.\n4. Write or extend a test first:\n   - Pure logic that does not need `core.php`: add a test in `tests/Unit/` and run `vendor/bin/phpunit -c phpunit.unit.xml --filter <TestName>`.\n   - Logic that needs the database: add a test in `tests/Mantis/` (extends `MantisCoreBase`). REST behaviour goes in `tests/rest/`.\n5. Make the change. Follow the conventions in AGENTS.md: tabs, `p_`/`t_`/`c_`/`f_`/`g_` prefixes, `require_api()` for core modules, user-visible text through `lang_get()` (see the `add-language-string` skill).\n6. Run the fast gate: `composer run check-fast`. Fix every failure. Do not skip or delete tests.\n7. If the change touches the database, a command, the REST or SOAP API, or a page flow, run the full gate: `composer run check` (needs Docker, reinstalls the local instance). To run one integration test after an install: `vendor/bin/phpunit --filter <TestName>`.\n8. If the schema changes, add an upgrade step at the end of `admin/schema.php`. Never edit existing steps.\n9. Commit with a short imperative subject, as the history does (`Fix tag cache invalidation`, then `Test tag cache invalidation`).\n10. Add an entry to `docs/harness/log.md` if you learned something that the next person needs. Open a pull request to `master`. Never push to `master` directly.\n","numLines":20,"startLine":1,"totalLines":20}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Rb8FsCmmLsvUatAeBX3pBc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
